 ","type":"text"},{"code":"translation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"velocity","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FIDELITY TODO: the exact default constants (Momentum Friction, Rubber Band Friction, decel rate)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"live as port default "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"values","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" inside origami.DragSettings — reading them needs FlatBuffers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"port-value decoding, which the parser doesn’t do yet. Until then the momentum decay uses the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s velocity projection ("},{"code":"predictedEndTranslation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") and rubber-band uses the iOS-standard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constant (0.55). Mark these for replacement once the parser extracts DragSettings’ real defaults."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"title":"Swami","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/docume